      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2001-p14.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(x\\) be what we are trying to find. \\(x-1=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{2}{1+\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{2}{1+\\ldots}}}} \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{x-1}-1=\\) \\(\\frac{2}{1+\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{2}{1+\\cdots}}} \\Rightarrow \\frac{2}{\\frac{1}{x-1}-1}=x \\Rightarrow x^{2}-2=0\\), so \\(x=\\sqrt{2}\\) since \\(x>0\\).",
